  OBSERVATION (not a FAIL, reported per the brief's "even if outside the
  manifest"): internal/services/mcpsvc/admin/undo.go:57 does
  `prior, ok := decisions[key]` as a pre-check before calling
  ClearDuplicateDecision. ClearDuplicateDecision (duplicate_decisions.go:134)
  correctly also looks under dl.legacyPairKeysFor(pairKey); undo.go's pre-check
  does not. So a pre-StableID decision still filed under its legacy PAIR key
  makes undo_resolve report "has no decision recorded against it" even though
